# Bundled FFmpeg/FFprobe sidecar binaries. Real binaries are large,
# platform-specific, and LGPL/GPL-licensed → never committed. `scripts/
# fetch-sidecars.*` downloads them here before `tauri build`.
#
# Tauri's externalBin requires the files to EXIST at build time (even for
# `cargo test` / `tauri dev`), so small placeholder stubs are committed so the
# context macro resolves. The Rust runtime ignores any binary smaller than
# 256 KiB (clearly a stub) and falls through to PATH — real FFmpeg binaries are
# multiple MB. Fetch scripts overwrite these stubs with real binaries.

# Ignore everything by default...
*

# ...except the gitignore, the README, and the placeholder stubs (which the
# fetch scripts overwrite with real binaries — those real binaries then match
# the `*` ignore and stay out of version control).
!.gitignore
!README.md
!ffmpeg-*-placeholder
!ffprobe-*-placeholder
!ffmpeg-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe
!ffprobe-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe
!ffmpeg-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe
!ffprobe-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe
!ffmpeg-x86_64-apple-darwin
!ffprobe-x86_64-apple-darwin
!ffmpeg-aarch64-apple-darwin
!ffprobe-aarch64-apple-darwin
!ffmpeg-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
!ffprobe-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
!ffmpeg-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
!ffprobe-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu